**Test filters.** For this step these gates run only the tests their filter selects (plus any inherited expected-red tests); put the tests this step adds or changes where a filter value finds them:
- `constructor-unit-tests`: 
- `ui-smoke`: 
- `ui-tests`: `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitWindowTests`, `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.SetupSaveLoadTests`

**How to implement.** The setup row saves the active setup and shows which setup the table draws (the S8.2 brief: 'the constructor's scene save / load becomes setup save / load'; 'The constructor model keeps the active setup and writes it through KitProxy'; 'editing a setup that an experiment uses mints the next revision'). Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S8.2. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs`. (a) `TableAndElementRotationMsg` gains `SaveSetup`, with a one-line doc: write the table over the active setup. (b) Its arm is refused by the read-only guard of step 185 like `CreateSetup`. With `activeSetupOpt = None` it writes nothing and sets `kitStatus` to `No setup is active: create one first.`. With `Some active`, the revised setup is `active.revisedWith (model.elements |> List.map (fun s -> s.recordedWith model.kitItems)) (active.pinFor model.experimentCollection.experiments)` (steps 256, 258 and 261): when it equals `active` nothing is written and `kitStatus` is `Setup '<name>' is unchanged.`; otherwise it is recorded through `recordSetup` (step 260): on `Ok`, `kitSetups` holds it in place of its name's, `activeSetupOpt` is `Some` it and `kitStatus` is `Saved setup '<name>', revision <n>.`; on `Error e` nothing else changes and `kitStatus` is `Not saved to the kit — <e.describe>`. (c) The view: the setup row (step 260) shows first, in a wrapping `TextBlock` carrying `ConstructorUiId.activeSetupText`, `Active setup: <name>, revision <n>` or, with none, `The table is not a setup of the kit yet.`; after `Create setup`, the `workbenchButton` `Save setup` (`ConstructorUiId.saveSetupButton`, dispatching `SaveSetup`), withheld (`availableWorkbenchButton`, step 185) when no setup is active or the kit is open read-only. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs`, beside step 260's setup-row ids, each with a one-line doc: `activeSetupText` (`"ActiveSetupText"`) and `saveSetupButton` (`"SaveSetupButton"`). No other message, field or id is added. Tests. `SetupModelTests` (step 260): `SaveSetup writes the active setup in place until an experiment references its revision, then mints the next`: after `CreateSetup` of `Bench` and the polarizer turned (`RotSetAxis (R1, BarDegrees 30.0)`), `SaveSetup` leaves `Bench` at revision 1 holding the turned slots; after `ExpChooseElement` of the polarizer and an `ExpCommit` over it (the table unchanged, so `Bench` stays at revision 1) and the polarizer turned again, `SaveSetup` gives `Bench` revision 2 with revision 1 in its history, the experiment still referencing revision 1, and `kitStatus` `Saved setup 'Bench', revision 2.`. `SaveSetup with no active setup, or over an unchanged table, writes nothing and says why`: with no active setup `SaveSetup` writes no setup file and sets `No setup is active: create one first.`; over an unchanged table it rewrites nothing (the file's bytes are unchanged) and sets `Setup 'Bench' is unchanged.`. `KitWindowModelTests` (step 185): `a kit opened read-only refuses every write message and writes nothing` also sends `SaveSetup` after a setup is active, with the same assertions. `SetupSaveLoadTests` (step 260): `the setup row renders its name field, Create setup and the saved setups` (trait `ui-smoke`) becomes `the setup row renders the active setup, its name field, Create setup, Save setup and the saved setups`, also holding `activeSetupText` and `saveSetupButton`; and `Save setup over a table an experiment uses keeps the earlier revision in the setup's kit file`: through the setup row's buttons and the Experiments bay's commit, a setup created, committed over and then saved changed holds both revisions in its `.setup-json`, read back through `readSetups`. `KitWindowTests` (step 185): `a read-only window withholds every write control` also finds no `saveSetupButton`.

**Acceptance.** After Save setup lands, `SaveSetup` MUST write the table over the active setup, in place until an experiment references its revision and as the next revision after, and refuse to write with no active setup, over an unchanged table or under a read-only kit, the setup row showing the active setup; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `SaveSetup writes the active setup in place until an experiment references its revision, then mints the next`, `SaveSetup with no active setup, or over an unchanged table, writes nothing and says why` and `a kit opened read-only refuses every write message and writes nothing`, the count rising by 2; ui-smoke MUST pass, including `the setup row renders the active setup, its name field, Create setup, Save setup and the saved setups`; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, including `Save setup over a table an experiment uses keeps the earlier revision in the setup's kit file` and `a read-only window withholds every write control`, the count rising by 1; and build, elevation and the fifteen s26 invariants MUST pass.
